  "reasoning": "The claim misrepresents the findings of a widely cited March 2023 Goldman Sachs research report. The report estimated that generative AI could expose the equivalent of 300 million full-time jobs globally to automation, not that 300 million jobs would be outright replaced. In the report's actual model, most exposed workers (approximately two-thirds of occupations) would have only a portion of their tasks automated and would see their work complemented by AI rather than substituted entirely. Furthermore, the report emphasized that technological displacement is historically offset by new job creation and estimated that generative AI could boost global GDP by 7%. Presenting the 300 million figure as a definitive prediction of direct job losses distorts the study's conclusions.",
